.env
*.db
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
dist/
.venv/
plan/
# Generated load-test artifacts (scenario copies + ramp campaigns)
**/.generated/
# Claude Code internal state (worktrees, transcripts, etc)
.claude/
logs/
# Job-mode artifacts (v3). Generated scenarios seeded from REAL production
# interactions, so these carry live customer PII by design — the metadata is
# what makes a faithful replication possible without test credentials.
# Never commit anything under here.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING: a bare `jobs/` matches a directory of that name
# at ANY depth, which silently excluded the job-mode SOURCE at `opkura/jobs/`.
# `/jobs/` anchors it to the repo root, which is the only place artifacts land.
/jobs/
# Client bot prompts — confidential per-client IP.
# Matches system-prompt.md at ANY depth under the repo (e.g. both
# clients/foo/system-prompt.md and clients/foo/bar/system-prompt.md).
# Previous single-`*` pattern only matched one level deep, which let
# clients/resurgent/system-prompt.md slip through.
**/system-prompt.md

# Client test data is NOT version-controlled.
#
# Every client directory holds identities lifted from production interactions so
# a test replicates the real call faithfully: names, registered phone numbers,
# SSN last-4, dates of birth, account numbers, addresses, email addresses. Same
# class of data as `jobs/`, so the same rule applies — never committed, never
# pasted into a ticket, never moved outside the repo.
#
# Blanket rather than per-directory on purpose. Classifying dir-by-dir was tried
# and it missed things: three real calls' `caller.wav` audio and interaction
# metadata sat committed under `logs/`, and two `variables.json` files held the
# source profiles everything else rendered from. A rule with no judgement call in
# it cannot be judged wrong, and it also covers the next client added by someone
# who has not read this file.
#
# Scenarios live at their natural paths (`clients/<client>/scenarios/...`) and
# simply are not tracked, so campaigns and relative references work unchanged.
#
# Two exceptions, both carrying no identities:
#   _examples/          reference scenarios to copy when writing a new one; the
#                       persona is invented (Iris Crawford), and
#                       tests/conftest.py loads happy-path.yaml
#   live-assistants.yaml  the guard list — assistant uuids and account COUNTS,
#                       no customer data. See scripts/refresh_live_assistants.py
#
# A negation cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the
# ignore is `clients/*` (matching entries, not the tree) and the exceptions name
# the directory itself.
clients/*
!clients/_examples
!clients/live-assistants.yaml
